# Refactor FolderSidebarView: Profile Registry Pattern

## Problem Statement

`buildSource()` in [folderSidebarView.svelte.ts](file:///Users/dduraipandian/apps/mdnotes/frontend/src/lib/views/folderSidebarView.svelte.ts) uses **scattered branching** to handle 5 different sidebar item behaviors (trash, favorites, home, regular, deleted). Every line branches on `kind`, `type`, `isViewTree`, `item.type`, or `item.deletedAt`. This makes it impossible to answer "what can a trash item do?" without reading 100+ lines.

**Goal**: Replace branching with a **Profile Registry** — a static lookup table where each sidebar kind declaratively describes its icon, capabilities, child strategy, and context menu. Then `buildSource()` becomes a simple linear assembler.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Do NOT create the Home folder as a new feature.** The `notes` system folder already exists in `systemFolders` (added by the user). This refactor just gives it a proper `home` profile so the system handles it correctly. Adding future system folders must be trivial: define a profile + add a kind mapping.

