## Phase 3: Refactor `FolderSidebarView` Methods

### Step 3.1: Add `resolveKind()` method

**File**: [folderSidebarView.svelte.ts](file:///Users/dduraipandian/apps/mdnotes/frontend/src/lib/views/folderSidebarView.svelte.ts)
**Location**: Inside the `FolderSidebarView` class, before `buildSource()`.

```typescript
private resolveKind(item: FolderItem): SidebarKind {
	if (item.deletedAt != null) return 'deleted';
	if (item.type === 'trash') return 'trash';
	if (item.id === 'favorites') return 'favorites';
	if (item.id === 'notes') return 'home';
	return 'regular';
}
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Order matters.** `deletedAt` check MUST come first, because a deleted regular folder should resolve to `'deleted'`, not `'regular'`. This is the **only place** where the kind is determined. All other methods just read `kind` from the profile.

### Step 3.2: Add `resolveChildIds()` method

**File**: [folderSidebarView.svelte.ts](file:///Users/dduraipandian/apps/mdnotes/frontend/src/lib/views/folderSidebarView.svelte.ts)
**Location**: Inside the class, after `resolveKind()`.

```typescript
private resolveChildIds(kind: SidebarKind, item: FolderItem): FolderID[] {
	switch (kind) {
		case 'trash':
			return this.folderQueries.getTrashRootIds();
		case 'favorites':
			return this.folderQueries.getFavoriteFolderIds();
		case 'deleted':
			return [];
		default:
			return item.items ?? [];
	}
}
```

**Rationale for each case**:
- `trash`: Children come from the trash index, not from `item.items`
- `favorites`: Children come from the favorites query, not from `item.items`
- `deleted`: Items inside trash intentionally don't show sub-folders (keeps trash flat)
- `default` (regular, home): Children come from `item.items` (real folder tree)

### Step 3.3: Refactor `buildSource()`

**File**: [folderSidebarView.svelte.ts](file:///Users/dduraipandian/apps/mdnotes/frontend/src/lib/views/folderSidebarView.svelte.ts)
**Location**: Replace the entire existing `buildSource()` method.

**Before** (current — 70 lines of branching):
```typescript
private buildSource(item: FolderItem, depth: number, isViewTree = false): SidebarSourceItem {
	const kind = item.type === 'trash' ? 'trash' : item.id === 'favorites' ? 'favorites' : 'regular';
	const type = kind === 'trash' || kind === 'favorites' ? 'view' : 'regular';
	const iconName: FolderIcon = kind === 'trash' ? 'trash' : kind === 'favorites' ? 'star' : 'folder';
	// ... 60+ more lines of branching ...
}
```

**After** (linear assembler — no branching):
```typescript
private buildSource(item: FolderItem, depth: number, suppressChildren = false): SidebarSourceItem {
	const kind = this.resolveKind(item);
	const profile = PROFILE_REGISTRY[kind];
	const iconConfig = ICON_REGISTRY[profile.iconName];

	const childIds = suppressChildren ? [] : this.resolveChildIds(kind, item);
	const visibleChildIds = childIds.filter(
		(id) => profile.showDeletedChildren || this.folders.folders.get(id)?.deletedAt == null
	);

	return {
		id: item.id,
		item,
		kind,
		icon: iconConfig.component,
		iconProps: iconConfig.props,
		title: item.title,
		depth,
		isSelected: this.selection.selectedFolderID === item.id,
		isEditing: this.folders.editingId === item.id,
		isOpen: item.isOpen ?? false,
		noteCount: this.noteQueries.getNoteCountForFolder(item.id, item.type),
		children: visibleChildIds
			.map((id) => this.folders.folders.get(id))
			.filter((child): child is FolderItem => !!child)
			.map((child) => this.buildSource(child, depth + 1, !profile.childrenExpandable)),
		capabilities: profile.capabilities,
		contextMenuItems: this.buildContextMenuItems(item, profile)
	};
}
```

**Key design decisions**:
1. `suppressChildren` replaces `isViewTree`. It means "you are inside a view that doesn't want sub-trees" (e.g., a regular folder shown under Favorites).
2. `!profile.childrenExpandable` is passed as `suppressChildren` to child calls. If the parent's profile says children can't expand, their grandchildren are suppressed.
3. `profile.showDeletedChildren` replaces the `kind === 'trash'` filter check — only trash shows deleted children.

### Step 3.4: Refactor `buildContextMenuItems()`

**File**: [folderSidebarView.svelte.ts](file:///Users/dduraipandian/apps/mdnotes/frontend/src/lib/views/folderSidebarView.svelte.ts)
**Location**: Replace the entire existing `buildContextMenuItems()` method.

**Before** (uses `capabilities` + `kind` + `item.type` checks):
```typescript
private buildContextMenuItems(
	item: FolderItem,
	capabilities: SidebarSourceItem['capabilities'],
	kind: string
): ContextMenuItem[] {
	// ... uses item.type !== 'system' && item.type !== 'trash' for favorites check
}
```

**After** (uses only `profile.capabilities`):
```typescript
private buildContextMenuItems(item: FolderItem, profile: SidebarProfileConfig): ContextMenuItem[] {
	const items: ContextMenuItem[] = [];
	const caps = profile.capabilities;

	if (caps.recover) {
		items.push({
			label: 'Recover Folder',
			action: () => this.actions.trashRecover(item.id),
			variant: 'default',
			separatorAfter: true
		});
		items.push({
			label: 'Delete Permanently',
			action: () => this.actions.trashPermanentDelete(item.title, item.id),
			variant: 'destructive',
			separatorAfter: false
		});
		return items;
	}

	if (caps.emptyTrash) {
		items.push({
			label: 'Empty Trash',
			action: () => this.actions.trashEmpty(),
			variant: 'destructive',
			separatorAfter: false
		});
		return items;
	}

	if (caps.create) {
		items.push({
			label: 'New Folder',
			action: () => this.actions.folderCreate(),
			variant: 'default',
			separatorAfter: false
		});
	}

	if (caps.favorite) {
		items.push({
			label: item.isFavorite ? 'Remove From Favorites' : 'Add To Favorites',
			action: () => this.actions.folderSetFavorite(item.id, item.isFavorite !== true),
			variant: 'default',
			separatorAfter: false
		});
	}

	if (caps.rename) {
		items.push({
			label: 'Rename',
			action: () => this.actions.folderStartRename(item.id),
			variant: 'default',
			separatorAfter: false
		});
	}

	if (caps.delete) {
		if (items.length > 0) {
			items[items.length - 1].separatorAfter = true;
		}
		items.push({
			label: 'Delete',
			action: () => this.actions.folderDelete(item.id),
			variant: 'destructive',
			separatorAfter: false
		});
	}

	return items;
}
```

> [!NOTE]
> The **only** change from the old code is replacing `if (item.type !== 'system' && item.type !== 'trash')` with `if (caps.favorite)`. All other logic is identical. The `favorite` capability is now declared in the profile, not computed from `item.type`.

